From 241e094542a5e61c296eb759eaeff9799067d5fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU613 <TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:15:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] distro: J714s pass in test-update-payload, J714s evidence
 in GAPS #23

test-update-payload.sh: when $M5_ARTIFACTS/t6050-j714s.dtb exists, build
and verify a payload with --board j714s, check that boot.bin carries the
apple,j714s DTB, and that the j716s verify then reports stale. Without
that file the script runs exactly as before (J716s only, same output).
It checks the board -> DTB path of m5pro-update-payload, not the DT.

GAPS.md #23: list the J714s results that exist elsewhere with their
labels (REPORTED 15/15 CPUs on a 27.3b1 stub; NATIVE on a different
kernel/loader: 1 CPU, keyboard/trackpad bind, hwmon, battery hang; no J714s
GPU result found in the sources reviewed) and the draft aurora J714s DT (omacom/linux-aurora #414).
None of these ran on this chain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 contrib/distro/GAPS.md                      | 2 +-
 contrib/distro/tools/test-update-payload.sh | 9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/contrib/distro/GAPS.md b/contrib/distro/GAPS.md
index 61e306d..8fd1b61 100644
--- a/contrib/distro/GAPS.md
+++ b/contrib/distro/GAPS.md
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ weeks, **L** <= 2 months, **XL** = new driver or upstream work with no date. "Ce
 | 20 | Stub refresh after macOS updates is manual and needs `recreate` + ceremony; firmware must be re-extracted to stay paired | `refresh-stub-firmware.sh:17-22`; `extract-tpmtfw.py:29-30` | installer "Refresh" action chaining recreate -> firmware -> known-good stage-1 -> ceremony; parameterise its size guards (lines 57, 79, 142) | S |
 | 21 | No backup of the M5 exists; the installer's resize is live APFS | `boot-and-recovery.md:244`, `:29-31` | installer requires an acknowledged backup (as omarchy-mac-installer does) | S |
 | 22 | Startup-disk switching from Linux (`asahi-bless`) and NVRAM access untested on M5; the stub stays the default boot volume, macOS only via power-hold | `bringup.md:157-159` | test `asahi-bless` read-only first | S |
-| 23 | J714s (14-inch) is untested on this chain; several tools default to J714s, the J716s work is the only hardware proof | `CHECKLIST.md` table | a J714s tester; board taken from the DT everywhere (`m5pro-update-payload` already does) | S + hardware |
+| 23 | J714s (14-inch) is untested on this chain; several tools default to J714s, the J716s work is the only hardware proof. Known J714s results elsewhere, none on this chain: REPORTED 15/15 CPUs, built-in keyboard and trackpad confirmed by hand, llvmpipe only (betizzel, recreated 27.3b1 stub, their own kernel and stage-1 m1n1; [linux-aurora #293](https://github.com/omacom/linux-aurora/issues/293#issuecomment-6700663901)); NATIVE on TripleU613's own asahi-wip 7.2 kernel and loader: 1 CPU (`maxcpus=1`, 26.x stub), keyboard/trackpad interfaces bound (separately, the owner confirmed keyboard typing and reported the trackpad working on that chain), 11 hwmon keys registered (the 2 battery keys were left out of that build), `macsmc-power` hard hang (kernel without omacom/linux-aurora #413's battery-string fix). No J714s GPU result found in the sources reviewed (the #293 thread, the omacom and aurora PRs, and this repository). Aurora-tree J714s DT: draft [omacom/linux-aurora #414](https://github.com/omacom/linux-aurora/pull/414), not booted | `CHECKLIST.md` table; `tools/test-update-payload.sh` runs a J714s pass when `t6050-j714s.dtb` is supplied (board-to-DTB path only) | a J714s tester; board taken from the DT everywhere (`m5pro-update-payload` already does) | S + hardware |
 | 24 | Packages, scripts and the hook were not run under `makepkg`/pacman (no aarch64 Arch here); only `bash -n`, `shellcheck`, and the payload builder against real artifacts in a fake ESP | this folder | `makepkg` + `namcap` in an aarch64 Arch container, then one install on the M5 over the tether | S |
 
 ## Shortest path to "someone else can install it"
diff --git a/contrib/distro/tools/test-update-payload.sh b/contrib/distro/tools/test-update-payload.sh
index 3cf628a..fe66ebe 100755
--- a/contrib/distro/tools/test-update-payload.sh
+++ b/contrib/distro/tools/test-update-payload.sh
@@ -21,4 +21,13 @@ if run verify; then echo "verify should report stale"; exit 1; fi
 run build; run status; run rollback
 printf '\x28\xb5\x2f\xfd' > "$S/z.img"; if run build --initramfs "$S/z.img" 2>/dev/null; then echo "zstd accepted"; exit 1; fi
 python3 -I "$here/mk-stage1.py" inspect "$S/esp/m1n1/boot.bin" | head -6
+# J714s (GAPS.md #23): same tool, --board j714s must pack t6050-j714s.dtb. Runs only when
+# $A/t6050-j714s.dtb exists; checks the board -> DTB path, not the DT's content.
+if [ -f "$A/t6050-j714s.dtb" ]; then
+    cp "$A/t6050-j714s.dtb" "$K/dtbs/apple/"
+    run14() { "$BASH5" "$U" --root "$S/root" --esp "$S/esp" --board j714s "$@"; }
+    run14 build; run14 verify
+    grep -qa 'apple,j714s' "$S/esp/m1n1/boot.bin" || { echo "j714s payload lacks the j714s DTB"; exit 1; }
+    if run verify; then echo "j716s verify should report stale after a j714s build"; exit 1; fi
+fi
 echo OK

